# .rgignore — ripgrep's own native ignore format (read unconditionally by
# ripgrep-based search, independent of .gitignore/.claudeignore detection).
#
# LS-8420: single-known-exact-path Glob() calls were observed timing out at
# the harness's 20s ripgrep budget in this monorepo, even though .gitignore
# and .claudeignore already exclude node_modules/ and .modules-pool/. The
# `Glob limitation on Windows worktrees` note in
# .agents/skills/mcp-first/SKILL.md documents the same underlying
# symlink-traversal quirk producing a different symptom (silent empty
# results) on Windows. Whatever code path skips gitignore-style detection
# (e.g. because it isn't reading git-repo config, or is resolving a worktree's
# node_modules symlink before applying name-based ignore rules) still reads
# .rgignore, since it is ripgrep's own convention and not a VCS integration.
# This file exists purely as defense-in-depth against that gap — keep it in
# sync with the heavy-directory entries in .gitignore / .claudeignore.

# Dependencies & generated output — the dominant source of file count in
# this repo (node_modules alone is ~95% of all files on disk).
node_modules/
.modules-pool/
dist/
build/
.next/
.expo/
.tamagui/
coverage/
.nx/cache
.nx/workspace-data
.turbo/
.vite/

# Ephemeral worktrees (each one symlinks node_modules into .modules-pool/).
.claude/worktrees/
.twig/

# VCS and lockfile noise
.git/
pnpm-lock.yaml
